  "boundary_evidence": [
    "One contiguous run of the Nitro SDK's SND_interface.c, 0x0205a86c..0x0205adf8: 28 functions, gapless in config/arm9/delinks.txt. Each is identified by its body against pret's pokediamond SND_interface.c: a PushCommand_impl call with the command's arguments, or an SNDi_SetPlayerParam/SNDi_SetTrackParam call with a field's offset and size. SND_StopTimer bumps the alarm ids first, SND_SetupAlarm sends SNDi_SetAlarmHandler's id, and SND_SetupCapture and SND_SetupChannelPcm pack their fields as pret's do. PushCommand_impl allocates a command, fills id and four arguments and pushes it.",
    "Order: mwccarm emits the bodies in reverse. PushCommand_impl, pret's static last function, is lowest and SND_StartSeq, pret's first, is highest. Between them the ROM keeps pret's order reversed. SND_SetTrackModDepth and SND_SetTrackModSpeed sit after SND_SetTrackPan, in the order of pret's SND_interface.h, and SND_SetTrackMute after SND_SetupAlarm, where pret's file leaves it as a comment, as it does SNDi_SetSurroundDecay after SNDi_SetTrackParam.",
    "Older SDK: no SND_PrepareSeq or SND_StartPreparedSeq, and command numbers below pret's. PauseSeq is 2, pret's 6..0x17 are 3 lower, pret's 0x19..0x1d (from SND_CMD_OUTPUT_SELECTOR, with no SND_CMD_MASTER_PAN before it) 4 lower, and the invalidate commands 3 lower again. Each number agrees with the function the body and position identify, and SND_CommandInit's set-shared-work command is 0x19, pret's 0x1d less 4.",
    "BOTTOM EDGE: SND_Init (0x0205a82c..0x0205a86c), SND_main.c's one function in this SDK.",
    "TOP EDGE: AllocCommand at 0x0205adf8, the lowest of SND_command.c (arm9/SND_Command)."
